# Files that must never reach a live deployment.
#
# Written after tools/anonymize-dev-db.php was deployed to production and found
# to run there: the host has APP_ENV=local and a loopback database, so the
# environment and host gates both passed. The tool now requires an explicit
# ANONYMIZE_ALLOW_DEV opt-in, but shipping a destructive development tool to a
# live server is a second mistake on its own. Keep it off the server as well.
.git/
node_modules/
.env
.bak/
*.bak
reports/
storage/private/*
# Development-only tooling and harnesses
tools/anonymize-dev-db.php
tests/
playwright.config.ts
design-system/

# Settings the portal writes at runtime.
#
# These are edited through the admin screens and live only on the server that
# owns them. They were being shipped from the repository on every deploy, so a
# change made in /admin/header survived until the next release and then
# silently reverted — which is what kept removing Events from the main menu.
#
# The copies in the repository stay as the starting point for a new
# installation; see docs/deploy/README.md.
config/announcements.json
config/holidays.json
config/chrome.json
config/church-info.json
config/hero.json
config/ministries.json
config/people.json
config/related-families.json
config/theme.json

# Server-owned deployment state. The maintenance flag is written on the server
# by tools/deploy.sh and cleared there; syncing a local copy would either take
# the site down or lift a gate that is still needed.
storage/maintenance.flag
